WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.700
MICHAEL J. SANDEL: Philosophy
estranges us from the familiar,

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:11.940
not by supplying new information,
but by inviting and provoking

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:13.050
a new way of seeing.

00:00:15.560 --> 00:00:22.490
But, and here's the risk, once
the familiar turns strange,

00:00:22.490 --> 00:00:25.820
it's never quite the same again.

00:00:25.820 --> 00:00:31.190
Self-knowledge is like lost innocence.

00:00:31.190 --> 00:00:38.555
However unsettling you find it, it
can never be unthought or unknown.

00:00:41.610 --> 00:00:48.070
What makes this enterprise
difficult but also riveting

00:00:48.070 --> 00:00:53.670
is that moral and political
philosophy is a story.

00:00:53.670 --> 00:00:55.700
And you don't know where
the story will lead,

00:00:55.700 --> 00:01:01.780
but what you do know is
that the story is about you.

